  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its proximity to substantial commercial plant, its reliance on&amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-6f8af669-7fff-3a08-bc1c-1fd85e3514bc&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;a Mechanical Ventilation Heat Recovery (MVHR) system, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;and permanently fixed-shut windows to mitigate noise, fails to demonstrate that the impact of noise from adjoining commercial premises on intended occupiers would be acceptable.&amp;nbsp; The proposal is therefore contrary to paragraphs 57, 135, 191, and 198 of the National Planning Policy Framework and Condition G.2(1)(e)(iii) of Class G, Part 3, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/p&gt;"
